.SH "NAME"
aerospace-list-apps \- Print the list of running applications that appears in the Dock and may have a user interface
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
aerospace list\-apps [\-h|\-\-help] [\-\-macos\-native\-hidden [no]] [\-\-format <output\-format>] [\-\-count] [\-\-json]
.fi
.br
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Print the list of running applications that appears in the Dock and may have a user interface
.sp
The command is useful to inspect list of applications to compose filter for on\-window\-detected callback
.SH "OPTIONS"
.sp
\-h, \-\-help
.RS 4
Print help
.RE
.sp
\-\-macos\-native\-hidden [no]
.RS 4
Filter results to only print hidden applications.
\f(CR[no]\fP inverts the condition
.RE
.sp
\-\-format <output\-format>
.RS 4
Specify output format. See "Output Format" section for more details.
Incompatible with \f(CR\-\-count\fP
.RE
.sp
\-\-count
.RS 4
Output only the number of apps.
Incompatible with: \f(CR\-\-format\fP, \f(CR\-\-json\fP
.RE
.sp
\-\-json
.RS 4
Output in JSON format.
Can be used in combination with \f(CR\-\-format\fP to specify which data to include into the json.
Incompatible with \f(CR\-\-count\fP
.RE
.SH "OUTPUT FORMAT"
.sp
Output format can be configured with optional \f(CR[\-\-format <output\-format>]\fP option.
\f(CR<output\-format>\fP supports \c
.URL "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/String_interpolation" "string interpolation" "."
.sp
If not specified, the default \f(CR<output\-format>\fP is:
.br
\f(CR%{app\-pid}%{right\-padding} | %{app\-bundle\-id}%{right\-padding} | %{app\-name}\fP
.sp
The following variables can be used inside \f(CR<output\-format>\fP:
.sp
%{app\-bundle\-id}
.RS 4
String. Application unique identifier. \c
.URL "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appstoreconnectapi/bundle_ids" "Bundle ID" ""
.RE
.sp
%{app\-name}
.RS 4
String. Application name
.RE
.sp
%{app\-pid}
.RS 4
Number. \c
.URL "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Process_identifier" "UNIX process identifier" ""
.RE
.sp
%{app\-exec\-path}
.RS 4
String. Application executable path
.RE
.sp
%{app\-bundle\-path}
.RS 4
String. Application bundle path
.RE
.sp
%{right\-padding}
.RS 4
A special variable which expands with a minimum number of spaces required to form a right padding in the appropriate column
.RE
.sp
%{newline}
.RS 4
Unicode U+000A newline symbol \f(CR\(rsn\fP
.RE
.sp
%{tab}
.RS 4
Unicode U+0009 tab symbol \f(CR\(rst\fP
.RE
